<%# What this study's status means for you.

    The "Your Match Factors" grid that used to sit here is gone. It read
    `score_breakdown` and rendered one box per factor -- age, sex, conditions,
    location, study type, risk -- which is the same six factors, from the same
    hash, that MatchScoreCardComponent draws as progress bars two panels above.
    The page said the same thing twice in two visual languages, once as a bar
    and once as a green or red box.

    The status sentence stays, and is the reason this component still exists.
    `get_study` is deliberately not filtered by status, so a saved study that has
    since completed still opens here, and "you cannot enroll" is the most
    important thing on the page when it applies. %>
<div id="what-this-means-for-you"
  class="border border-line-2 dark:border-line-on-dark rounded-panel p-8"
  role="region"
  aria-labelledby="status-message-title"
>
  <%= render Typography::HeadingComponent.new(size: :section, text: "What this means for you") %>

  <% if status_message.present? %>
    <p
      class="text-ink-2 dark:text-ink-2-on-dark text-base leading-relaxed"
      aria-label="<%= aria_label %>"
    >
      <%= status_message %>
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>
